{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgApS2NPpFqNqCzPFHEGY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night; the script fails, and then crashes before it can send the failure message. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` (one per night since you loaded it on 10-12) and `last exit code = 1`. The error log repeats two lines on every run, which point to two bugs on top of each other:\n\n1. **\"Not logged in · Please run /login\" is the root cause.** The plist only sets `PATH`, so `USER` isn't set when launchd runs the job. Without it, `claude` can't find its login in the keychain and quits. It works when you run it by hand because your terminal sets `USER`.\n2. **\"read-only variable: status\" is why you heard nothing.** In zsh, `status` is a built-in you can't assign to, and trying kills the script. That line comes after the failed `claude` call and before the `notify.sh` call, so the failure message was never sent.\n\n**Fixes:**\n- **Plist:** added `USER=vk` and `HOME=/Users/vk` to the environment.\n- **Script:**\n  - `status=$?` is now `rc=$?`.\n  - The prompt goes to `claude` on stdin.\n  - Each run logs its exit code and how long it took to the error log.\n  - An empty review now counts as a failure, even if `claude` exits 0.\n  - If `notify.sh` itself fails, that's written to the error log too.\n\n**Testing:** I ran both versions in a stripped-down environment like launchd's, with fake `claude` and `notify.sh`. The original sends nothing when `claude` fails. The fixed version sends a failure message when `claude` fails or produces no output, and the summary when it works. The plist and script also pass syntax checks. I haven't run it on your real machine; this folder is only a snapshot.\n\n**What you need to do:** copy the two files into place and reload the job (`launchctl bootout`, then `bootstrap`; plist changes need a reload). Then run it now with `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review` and check:\n- the exit code is 0\n- today's review file isn't empty\n- the run took a believable time, not 0–2 seconds\n- the summary arrived on Telegram\n\nThen break it once on purpose and check that the failure message arrives. If it still says \"Not logged in\" with `USER` set, use `claude setup-token` instead. The exact steps are in ANSWER.md.\n\n**Colleague's note:** the `status` bug, the `USER` / \"Not logged in\" fix, \"check `launchctl print` and the error log first\" and \"exit 0 isn't proof it worked\" all matched exactly. Their \"Input must be provided\" error doesn't appear in your log, so sending the prompt on stdin is only a precaution here. ANSWER.md lists which parts applied."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2030,"cache_read_input_tokens":26811,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2030},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a5d509d-2131-42a4-b01a-3be46fd8493d","uuid":"282d86a1-33d5-47d5-ac23-56ddf8ffd048","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:37:23.546Z","request_id":"req_011CgApS1yqKXRjUb7aidaQW"}
